// # AArch64 Tier 0 Closure Plan
//
// Logline: Identifies the three concrete ports needed to close the Tier 0 0-matcher gap, with file shape, line budget, dependencies, and named lock for each.
//
// Setup: Reads ROADMAP.oot §5.2 Tier 0 row and the existing x86_emit_list.oo / oodac/aarch64_emit_*.oo sources to derive the porting surface.
//
// Beats:
//   1. List[T] port — the highest-impact missing port.
//   2. no_output detector — closes the silent no-op main class.
//   3. 5-shape refuse gate — refuses hostile shapes before emit.
//   4. The chs_rt OoRes_S collision blocker.
//   5. Verification plan.

File: openOODA/audit/aarch64-tier0-closure.oot
Status: open — 2026-08-26 plan for the next worker.
Context: Read-only audit. No .oo files were modified by this audit itself.

---

## 1. List[T] port (highest impact)

The 54 aarch64_*.oo fixtures do not use List[T], so the missing port
does not break current tests. But the 0-matcher gap closure requires
List[T] to match the x86 parity per ROADMAP.oot §5.2.

Source to port: `oodac/x86_emit_list.oo` (134 lines).

Target: `oodac/aarch64_emit_list.oo` (cap 256 lines).

Required changes:
- Replace SysV `call list_new@PLT` with AAPCS64 `bl list_new` (x0
  return, no args).
- Replace `mov %rdi, %rsi` arg sequencing with `mov x0, x1` AAPCS64
  arg passing.
- Replace `x86_runtime_text()` AT&T prologue with AArch64 frame
  prologue `stp x29, x30, [sp, #-N]!; mov x29, sp; ...; ldp x29, x30,
  [sp], #N; ret`.
- Reuse `aarch64_emit_heap.oo`'s brk-based `_alloc` / `_free` for
  any heap needs (or rely on `.bss` for the static list_oob_msg).

Lock: `scripts/aarch64_list_smoke.oo` that runs oodac.aarch64 on
fixtures/aarch64_list_int.oo (new fixture) and asserts the
`println(list_len(xs))` output equals the expected length.

## 2. no_output detector

The x86 backend has `x86_emit_no_output.oo` (117 lines) that
detects the silent no-op main class (binary exits 0 with empty
stdout). The aarch64 backend has no equivalent. Without it, a
correctly-typed main that prints nothing is indistinguishable from
a miscompile.

Target: `oodac/aarch64_emit_no_output.oo` (cap 256 lines).

Required changes: re-shape the x86 `wr_bytes != 0` invariant to
the AArch64 `svc #0, x8, SYS_write` exit-check invariant. After
the new `svc #0` for exit, check that `_start` contains a `mov x0,
#1; mov x1, address; mov x2, length; mov x8, #64; svc #0` write
sequence to stdout. If absent and the user has a `println` in main,
the detector fails closed.

Lock: `scripts/aarch64_no_output_smoke.oo` that runs oodac.aarch64
on a no-println fixture and asserts the post-`_start` invariant
fires.

## 3. 5-shape refuse gate

The x86 backend has `x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo` (238 lines) that
detects the 5 silent-miscompile shapes (Float usage, 3-arm match,
Result[T], struct field/type, List[T]) and fails closed before
emit. The aarch64 backend relies on per-shape `return []` and the
final `leftover` check in `a64_collect_prints`.

Target: `oodac/aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo` (cap 256 lines).

Required changes: port the 5-shape signature scan. Each shape
gets one `pub fn aarch64_emit_shape_refuse_test(src) -> List<String>`
that returns an ERR list. The dispatch in aarch64_emit.oo calls all
5 before the dispatch ladder, `process_exit(1)` on any non-empty
err.

Lock: `scripts/aarch64_shape_refuse_smoke.oo` that runs the 5
test shapes (5 fixtures) through the gate and asserts all 5 ERR.

## 4. chs_rt OoRes_S collision (blocker for in-process smokes)

The C emit at `oodac/c_emit_preamble.oo:52` emits
`typedef OoResS OoRes_S;` as an alias, but a downstream C emit
file generates `typedef struct OoRes_S { ... } OoRes_S;` which
conflicts. The two typedefs must be reconciled: either drop the
alias when the struct is defined later in the same translation
unit, or rename the struct consistently to `OoResS` everywhere.

Fix lives in `oodac/c_emit_*.oo` and affects every `ooda run`
compilation.

## 5. Verification plan

After each port:
1. `ooda/scripts/<name>_smoke.oo` typechecks OK.
2. The smoke runs the new fixture and reports pass.
3. `./bin/ooda run ../openOODA/scripts/enforcer.oo` returns
   8/8 green.
4. The audit `openOODA/audit/aarch64-neon-abi-and-enforcer.oot`
   gets a new section recording the port and the lock.

After all 3 ports + chs_rt fix:
- 54/54 aarch64 fixtures run through the no_output detector.
- 54/54 aarch64 fixtures pass the 5-shape refuse gate.
- 3+ List[T] fixtures compile and run via qemu-aarch64.
- 8/8 enforcer gates green.
